1. plots theoretical rate–distortion curves;

2. solves a toy Information Bottleneck problem with self-consistent iterations;

3. verifies the exact decomposition of VAE rate into mutual information and prior mismatch.

Answer:

- why the IB representation is trivial at small $\beta$;
- why $I(T;Y)$ saturates before $I(X;T)$;
- how a poor prior increases KL-rate without adding information about the input.
